paras.en:
Now my power over speech is somewhat shut;
my nature stays shut in thought night and day.
The river of speech, the flow of thought, is wave-barred (blocked);
how should the tongue not be shut again and again in the mouth
when the livelihood of the people of Agra is shut?

Unemployment has shown this poverty;
it is not the roof of the house, it is poverty that has spread over it.
Poverty has entered between wall and door;
in every home poverty has filled up in such a way
as the flow of water breaks off once and is shut.

By labour not a cowrie comes to hand or foot;
how long can anyone idle live on loans and credit?
Whomever I see, he keeps crying “alas, alas”;
at such a state, alas, we too feel like weeping;
may God not shut even an enemy’s business.
